  "title": "2026-09-08-comp-134600 · code-review-agents",
  "description": "# Multi-agent automated code review\nRead left to right: intake resolves PR inputs and rejects drafts / excludes generated and vendored paths before model work. Budgeted context ranks source, hunks, tests, ownership and review history, logging omissions. The planner partitions work and fans out to five concurrent reviewers; their shared contract specifies read-only tools, call budgets and structured findings.\n\nResults merge into deduplication, severity reconciliation, confidence filtering and current-head location checks. High-severity findings are rechecked against source; unverified findings are demoted and withheld. Survivors become inline comments and a policy-driven verdict.\n\nThe lower control band documents head-change cancellation, partial-work disposal and restart on the new head. Publication feeds author replies and reviewer disagreements into calibration: wrong findings are recorded and class confidence thresholds inform later aggregation. Telemetry tracks cost, latency, reviewer tokens, cancellations and acceptance/dismissal; daily budget overruns limit subsequent reviews to correctness and security.",
  "mode": "diagram",
